    <worksheet name='Discount vs Profit Scatter Plot'>
      <layout-options>
        <caption>
          <formatted-text>
            <run>DESCRIPTION
The graph depicts the correlation between discount percentages and profits in individual retail orders.
Circles represent each order; their size stands for sales value while color indicates the category of goods.


ANALYSIS / BUSINESS PERSPECTIVE
The graph is useful to the marketing department to figure out if the increased discount leads to profits 
or to bigger losses. Big circles located below the break-even point stand for orders which yielded losses and
should be analyzed.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </caption>
      </layout-options>
      <table>
        <view>
          <datasources>
            <datasource caption='Sample - Superstore' name='federated.0xgffwl0x9lrlw1g0nbqy1vzka5g' />
