    <worksheet name='KPI -Total Profit '>
      <layout-options>
        <caption>
          <formatted-text>
            <run>DESCRIPTION
This KPI measures the overall profit that results from the profitability of all orders that fall under the chosen view.

ANALYSIS / BUSINESS PERSPECTIVE
Overall Profit indicates whether the sales are profitable. High sales with low profits might suggest either too much discounting or poor sales mix, which is why this KPI should be read alongside Total Sales at all times.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </caption>
      </layout-options>
      <table>
        <view>
          <datasources>
            <datasource caption='Sample - Superstore' name='federated.0xgffwl0x9lrlw1g0nbqy1vzka5g' />
          </datasources>
