    <worksheet name='Monthly Sales and Profit Trend '>
      <layout-options>
        <caption>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true'>DESCRIPTION</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true'>In this chart, there is a line graph with two lines that show monthly sales and profit. The line for sales is a measure of demand from customers, and the other line indicates profits during that period of time.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true'>ANALYSIS / BUSINESS PERSPECTIVE</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true'>From this chart, the marketing department can recognize growth trends as well as seasonality of peaks, </run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true'>and also when the sales and profits change differently. When there is a month that shows high sales and low profits, it means that there might have been too many discounts or low margin products sold.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </caption>
      </layout-options>
      <table>
        <view>
          <datasources>
            <datasource caption='Sample - Superstore' name='federated.0xgffwl0x9lrlw1g0nbqy1vzka5g' />
          </datasources>
          <datasource-dependencies datasource='federated.0xgffwl0x9lrlw1g0nbqy1vzka5g'>
            <column datatype='date' name='[Order Date]' role='dimension' type='ordinal' />
            <column datatype='real' name='[Profit]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
            <column datatype='real' name='[Sales]' role='measure' type='quantitative' />
            <column datatype='string' name='[Segment]' role='dimension' type='nominal' />
            <column-instance column='[Profit]' derivation='Sum' name='[sum:Profit:qk]' pivot='key' type='quantitative' />
            <column-instance column='[Sales]' derivation='Sum' name='[sum:Sales:qk]' pivot='key' type='quantitative' />
            <column-instance column='[Order Date]' derivation='Month-Trunc' name='[tmn:Order Date:qk]' pivot='key' type='quantitative' />
          </datasource-dependencies>
          <filter class='categorical' column='[federated.0xgffwl0x9lrlw1g0nbqy1vzka5g].[Action (Segment)]'>
            <groupfilter function='level-members' level='[Segment]' user:ui-action-filter='[Action1_74EB87C9B02F40A8A39D8F4821129353]' user:ui-enumeration='all' user:ui-marker='enumerate' />
          </filter>
          <filter class='quantitative' column='[federated.0xgffwl0x9lrlw1g0nbqy1vzka5g].[tmn:Order Date:qk]' included-values='in-range-or-null'>
            <min>#2014-01-01 00:00:00#</min>
            <max>#2016-12-14 23:59:59#</max>
          </filter>
          <slices>
            <column>[federated.0xgffwl0x9lrlw1g0nbqy1vzka5g].[tmn:Order Date:qk]</column>
            <column>[federated.0xgffwl0x9lrlw1g0nbqy1vzka5g].[Action (Segment)]</column>
          </slices>
          <aggregation value='true' />
        </view>
        <style>
          <style-rule element='axis'>
            <encoding attr='space' class='0' field='[federated.0xgffwl0x9lrlw1g0nbqy1vzka5g].[sum:Profit:qk]' field-type='quantitative' fold='true' scope='rows' type='space' />
          </style-rule>
          <style-rule element='quick-filter'>
