            <zone h='74274' id='5' paired-zone-id='4' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard' w='99000' x='500' y='24896'>
              <flipboard active-id='4' nav-type='caption' show-nav-arrows='true'>
                <story-points>
                  <story-point caption='Determines regions where there is high customer demand as opposed to low customer demand for effective marketing and expansion strategies.' captured-sheet='Regional Sales' id='4' />
                  <story-point caption='Indicates that higher discounts can make sales profitable or cause losses, allowing managers to pinpoint loss-generating transactions and set levels for profitable discounting.' captured-sheet='Discount vs Profit Scatter Plot' id='3' />
                  <story-point caption='Identifies areas that have high volumes but low profitability, thus areas with high sales that are affected by low margins owing to discounts, high transport costs, or poor product mix.' captured-sheet='Sales and profit by region' id='2' />
                  <story-point caption='The Regional and Discount oppertunities dashboard is a transition from the company’s and customer’s performance to geographical and price considerations. It reveals locations of sales, evaluates regional sales against profits and analyzes &#10;whether the level of discount can be related to either profit or loss.&#10;&#10;This dashboard transforms sales information into geographical and price decisions. It identifies &#10;locations of demand, checks whether each region is able to make a profit from sales and finds whether &#10;discounts are the cause of loss.' captured-sheet='Regional and Discount Oppertunities' id='1'>
